    updated_at: 'JAMB • WAEC Official Syllabus',
    content: `<h1 style="text-align:center"><strong>L'Identité (Identity)</strong></h1>
<h2><strong>Objectives</strong></h2>
<p>By the end of this lesson, students should be able to:</p>
<ol>
<li>Introduce themselves and others in French.</li>
<li>Ask and answer questions about personal information.</li>
<li>Use appropriate vocabulary related to identity.</li>
</ol>
<h2><strong>Lesson Content</strong></h2>
<p><strong>1. Les Salutations (Greetings)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bonjour !</strong> – Hello / Good morning!</li>
<li><strong>Bonsoir !</strong> – Good evening!</li>
<li><strong>Salut !</strong> – Hi! (informal)</li>
<li><strong>Comment ça va ?</strong> – How are you?</li>
<li><strong>Ça va bien, merci.</strong> – I'm fine, thank you.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>2. Se Présenter (Introducing Oneself)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Je m'appelle...</strong> – My name is...</li>
<li><strong>J'ai... ans.</strong> – I am... years old.</li>
<li><strong>Je suis étudiant(e).</strong> – I am a student.</li>
<li><strong>Je viens de...</strong> – I come from...</li>
<li><strong>J'habite à...</strong> – I live in...</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>3. Poser des Questions Personnelles (Asking Personal Questions)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Comment tu t'appelles ?</strong> – What is your name?</li>
<li><strong>Quel âge as-tu ?</strong> – How old are you?</li>
<li><strong>D'où viens-tu ?</strong> – Where are you from?</li>
<li><strong>Où habites-tu ?</strong> – Where do you live?</li>
<li><strong>Quelle est ta nationalité ?</strong> – What is your nationality?</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>4. Les Informations Personnelles (Personal Information)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Le nom</strong> – Last name</li>
<li><strong>Le prénom</strong> – First name</li>
<li><strong>L'âge</strong> – Age</li>
<li><strong>La date de naissance</strong> – Date of birth</li>
<li><strong>Le lieu de naissance</strong> – Place of birth</li>
<li><strong>L'adresse</strong> – Address</li>
<li><strong>Le numéro de téléphone</strong> – Phone number</li>
<li><strong>La nationalité</strong> – Nationality</li>
<li><strong>La profession</strong> – Occupation</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>5. Les Nationalités (Nationalities)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Nigérian/Nigériane</strong> – Nigerian</li>
<li><strong>Ghanéen/Ghanéenne</strong> – Ghanaian</li>
<li><strong>Français/Française</strong> – French</li>
<li><strong>Américain/Américaine</strong> – American</li>
<li><strong>Britannique</strong> – British</li>
</ul>
<p><em>Note: Nationalities in French are capitalized when used as nouns but not when used as adjectives.</em><strong>6. Les Professions (Occupations)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Étudiant/Étudiante</strong> – Student</li>
<li><strong>Enseignant/Enseignante</strong> – Teacher</li>
<li><strong>Médecin</strong> – Doctor</li>
<li><strong>Ingénieur</strong> – Engineer</li>
<li><strong>Commerçant/Commerçante</strong> – Trader</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>7. Les Pronoms Personnels (Personal Pronouns)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Je</strong> – I</li>
<li><strong>Tu</strong> – You (informal)</li>
<li><strong>Il</strong> – He</li>
<li><strong>Elle</strong> – She</li>
<li><strong>Nous</strong> – We</li>
<li><strong>Vous</strong> – You (formal/plural)</li>
<li><strong>Ils</strong> – They (masculine or mixed group)</li>
<li><strong>Elles</strong> – They (feminine)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>8. Les Verbes Essentiels (Essential Verbs)</strong><strong>Être (To be)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Je suis</strong> – I am</li>
<li><strong>Tu es</strong> – You are</li>
<li><strong>Il/Elle est</strong> – He/She is</li>
<li><strong>Nous sommes</strong> – We are</li>
<li><strong>Vous êtes</strong> – You are</li>
<li><strong>Ils/Elles sont</strong> – They are</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Avoir (To have)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>J'ai</strong> – I have</li>
<li><strong>Tu as</strong> – You have</li>
<li><strong>Il/Elle a</strong> – He/She has</li>
<li><strong>Nous avons</strong> – We have</li>
<li><strong>Vous avez</strong> – You have</li>
<li><strong>Ils/Elles ont</strong> – They have</li>
</ul>`
